# FDA-approved samples stay in git

`samples/fda_approved.sdf` and `samples/fda_approved.cms` are project samples. If either file is untracked or modified, commit it and push it to GitHub with the branch. Do not treat them as local-only sample data.

- Commit both files when they change. They are one sample set and may share a commit.
- Leave `*.mctcache` untracked. Those sidecars are a local render cache, including `samples/fda_approved.mctcache` and `samples/fda_approved.cms.mctcache`.
- Other large extracts under `samples/` stay untracked unless a request names them.
